// Waterbirth Dungeon maze - ambient/filler combat npcs (m28_68/m29_68/m30_68). Migrated from the raw
// 377 cache dump (content/scripts/_unpack/377/all.npc), same pattern as this folder's own
// dagannoth_kings.npc: base appearance/model/anim fields above "op2=Attack" are the untouched raw
// cache values (including a couple of the cache's own quirks, like jb_baby_dagganoth's duplicated
// resizeh/resizev lines - kept verbatim rather than "cleaned up"); everything from op2=Attack onward
// is new, wiring these into skill_combat. Corey (2026-09-03): "all of the npcs in the maze need to be
// aggressive, they all also need their correct attacks, defense, hp, etc".
//
// Real identities confirmed via the OSRS wiki, not assumed from the cache's own tag/name text:
// - dungeon_dagganoth_lighter_deeper (raw vislevel=88) and dungeon_dagganoth_mainroom_deeper (raw
//   vislevel=90) ARE the two real "Dagannoth (Waterbirth Island)" variants - ranged and melee
//   respectively (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dagannoth_(Waterbirth_Island)) - it's the raw
//   vislevel matching the wiki's exact combat levels (88/90) that confirmed this, not the cache's
//   generic "lighter"/"mainroom" tag names.
// - giant_rockcrab_deeper (vislevel=137) is the real, already-revealed Giant Rock Crab
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Giant_Rock_Crab).
// - dagannoth_rock_lobster_2x2 (vislevel=127 - NOT the same tag as the placed "_2x2_loc" variant, see
//   below) is the real, already-revealed Rock Lobster (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Rock_lobster).
// - dungeon_dagganoth_magic_monster_deeper is actually Wallasalki (real name="Wallasalki" already in
//   the raw cache block) - not a Dagannoth at all despite the tag name. A distinct magic attacker
//   genuinely native to the Waterbirth Island Dungeon per the wiki
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Wallasalki - "much stronger than their combat level suggests").
// - jb_baby_dagganoth is the real Dagannoth fledgeling
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Dagannoth_fledgeling) - wiki-confirmed **NOT aggressive**,
//   an intentional exception to "make them all aggressive" to match real behaviour (flagged for Corey
//   to override if he'd rather every single one be hostile regardless).
//
// Explicitly NOT migrated here, left untouched in all.npc:
// - giant_rockcrab_hidden_deeper ("Boulder") and dagannoth_rock_lobster_2x2_loc ("Rock") - both
//   vislevel=hide with NO op2 at all in the raw cache (unlike the door-support npcs earlier this
//   project, which had vislevel=hide but a real op2 already). all.seq has real
//   horror_crab_hide/_reveal and dagannoth_rock_lobster_spring_up sequences, confirming these ARE
//   meant to be disguise states that transform into the real monster on interaction (the same
//   mechanic as regular rock crabs) - but that transform trigger isn't scripted anywhere yet, and
//   isn't attempted this pass. Flagged rather than guessed at: per the project doc's original map
//   sweep, it's the DISGUISED "_loc"/hidden forms that are actually placed in the maze (14 instances
//   of dagannoth_rock_lobster_2x2_loc in m30_68 alone) - so until the reveal mechanic is built,
//   players may not actually encounter a fightable Rock Lobster or hidden Rock Crab there, even
//   though the real fightable forms below are now fully wired.
// - jb_viking_dude ("Bardur") - a real, named, ordinarily-friendly Fremennik NPC
//   (https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Bardur): "resides deep within the Waterbirth Island Dungeon,
//   where he fights dagannoth fledgelings" (this exact room), tied to The Fremennik
//   Exiles/Trials quests, non-hostile since a 2019 update "to make it easier to talk to him". His raw
//   vislevel=94 matches his old pre-2019 attackable combat level exactly, confirming he's genuine
//   period content, just not a "make it aggressive" filler monster - left alone.

[dungeon_dagganoth_magic_monster_deeper]
name=Wallasalki
desc=A fearsome magical water creature.
model1=npc_2457
walkanim=wallasalki_walk
readyanim=wallasalki_ready
resizeh=110
resizev=110
op2=Attack
vislevel=98
huntmode=cowardly
huntrange=6
hitpoints=120
attack=1
strength=1
defence=80
magic=100
ranged=1
param=magicattack,100
param=stabdefence,100
param=slashdefence,150
param=crushdefence,175
param=magicdefence,250
param=rangedefence,-10
param=damagetype,^magic_style
param=attackrate,6
param=attackrange,7
param=magicattack_anim,wallasalki_attack
param=defend_anim,wallasalki_defend
param=death_anim,wallasalki_death
param=retreat,0

[giant_rockcrab_deeper]
